    "text": "To determine the speed at which Marcos needs to travel across the 5-mile lake in 10 minutes, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Convert the time from minutes to hours:**\n   Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, we convert 10 minutes to hours by dividing by 60:\n   \\[\n   10 \\text{ minutes} = \\frac{10}{60} \\text{ hours} = \\frac{1}{6} \\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the speed:**\n   Speed is defined as the distance traveled divided by the time taken. Here, the distance is 5 miles and the time is \\(\\frac{1}{6}\\) hours. So, the speed \\(v\\) is:\n   \\[\n   v = \\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}} = \\frac{5 \\text{ miles}}{\\frac{1}{6} \\text{ hours}} = 5 \\times 6 = 30 \\text{ miles per hour}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, Marcos needs to travel at a speed of \\(\\boxed{30}\\) miles per hour to make it to work on time.",
